00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.280
- I was gonna say, yeah, you're so funny,

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:07.170
and innately witty, you and Kenan.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:08.977
And I'm always like,
"What did y'all grow up on

00:02:08.977 --> 00:02:11.287
"that you ended up just
morphing into these beings

00:02:11.287 --> 00:02:13.170
"that make people laugh
everywhere you go?"

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:14.430
- Yeah, also my family too,

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:15.920
and the people around me in Chicago.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:17.850
A lot of my characters are based on that,

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:19.230
even one of my coaches.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:20.580
- Do they hate that or love that?

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:23.255
- Oh, well, I had a coach
that was after me (laughs)

00:02:23.255 --> 00:02:24.490
(audience laughs)

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:26.520
'cause I had a character
called Coach Kreeton,

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.170
and it was based on a coach in Chicago

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:29.550
and he was just mean all the time.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:30.922
It could be Valentine's,
(audience laughs)

00:02:30.922 --> 00:02:33.558
and he'd be like, "I
don't care about no love."

00:02:33.558 --> 00:02:35.930
"Sit down, shut up!"
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:37.350
He was loud like that.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:39.046
- I had a coach like that.
- Yeah!

00:02:39.046 --> 00:02:39.879
And I was like,

00:02:39.879 --> 00:02:42.060
"What is wrong with you?"
- "Run laps!"

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:43.147
You're feeling sad, they're like, "Run,

00:02:43.147 --> 00:02:44.040
"it'll make you feel better."

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.030
No it won't.
(audience laughs)

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.140
It will not, actually.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.160
- Right!
- I hear another one

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.170
of your influences, though,
was George Clinton, right?

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:52.068
- George, oh come on, now,
Parliament-Funkadelic?

00:02:52.068 --> 00:02:53.100
(audience cheers)
You know what I mean?

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.048
Oh, hey! (laughs)

00:02:55.048 --> 00:02:57.810
And my dad had all the records.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:59.940
He had a little man cave in the basement

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:01.137
in Chicago.
- Love it.

00:03:01.137 --> 00:03:02.490
- And he had all those records,

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.020
and I would listen to all of them.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:05.700
And then in "Good Burger" 1,

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.440
I got to meet George Clinton

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.208
and do the big dance scene.

00:03:09.208 --> 00:03:10.740
And he's in part two, too.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:11.899
Yeah, yeah, we got him back.

00:03:11.899 --> 00:03:12.808
- He had to get back.

00:03:12.808 --> 00:03:14.370
- He's in "Good Burger 2," yeah.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:15.600
- Do y'all improvise a lot?

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.010
I feel like, 'cause Kenan,

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:18.330
